{
  "schema_version": 5,
  "type": "bugfix",
  "problem": [
    {
      "text": "The extension source list previously embedded absolute checkout paths in the build configuration.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_36a41d29dcbb427c8d802ad385e5f6e4"]
    }
  ],
  "reasoning": [
    {
      "text": "Expressing source paths relative to setup.py removes the checkout-specific absolute prefix while retaining the discovered source files.",
      "basis": "source",
      "evidence": ["call_36a41d29dcbb427c8d802ad385e5f6e4"]
    }
  ],
  "impact": [
    {
      "text": "This makes extension source metadata independent of the checkout's absolute location under the usual project-root invocation.",
      "basis": "inference",
      "evidence": ["call_36a41d29dcbb427c8d802ad385e5f6e4", "call_8bfa10371fc14652be7b1e44b2b52bb8"]
    }
  ],
  "source_notes": [],
  "limitations": [
    "No package installation, distribution build or native compilation was run; compatibility improvements are inferred rather than measured.",
    "Source discovery still starts from a working-directory-relative directory. The change does not establish support for invoking setup.py from arbitrary working directories."
  ],
  "links": [],
  "chapters": [
    {
      "id": "build-source-paths",
      "title": "Relative extension source paths",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "The source-list comprehension still walks exllamav3/exllamav3_ext and selects .c, .cpp and .cu files. Only path normalization changes: abspath becomes relpath with os.path.dirname(__file__) as its base.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_36a41d29dcbb427c8d802ad385e5f6e4", "call_ba2e8f8a006c40c590bb8d69a4161909"]
        },
        {
          "text": "The resulting list feeds PyTorch's CUDAExtension when Torch is available and EXLLAMA_NOCOMPILE is absent. Compiler flags, source filtering and the precompilation gate remain unchanged.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_ba2e8f8a006c40c590bb8d69a4161909", "call_36a41d29dcbb427c8d802ad385e5f6e4"]
        },
        {
          "text": "A standard-library path-expression check modeled project-root invocation using both relative and absolute setup.py filenames. For bindings.cpp, the new expression produced a relative path resolving to the same target as the old absolute path. This checked path arithmetic, not the packaging implementation.",
          "basis": "execution",
          "evidence": ["call_8bfa10371fc14652be7b1e44b2b52bb8"]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "findings": [],
  "summary": "Changes native extension source paths from absolute checkout paths to paths relative to setup.py, without changing source selection or compilation settings."
}
